cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this tool informs a paper, a thesis, a lecture or a studio brief, please cite it as software."
type: software
title: "Solar Analysis Lab: A browser-based sun path and solar irradiance tool"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
abstract: >-
  A sun path and solar irradiance tool for architecture students that runs
  entirely in the browser, shipped as a single self-contained HTML file. The sun
  is moved through the day and the year over a massing model, with shadows cast
  in real time and the path drawn in 3D or as a stereographic projection.
  Geometry can be imported or built from OpenStreetMap buildings over a map
  basemap, and climate taken from an EPW file or, with none loaded, from a
  clear-sky model. A grid of sensors then reports solar irradiance in W/m² and
  cumulative radiation in kWh/m² on every surface, computed by ray tracing
  against a bounding-volume hierarchy in a worker, with the sky discretised over
  Tregenza/Reinhart patches under the Perez all-weather model. The method notes
  in docs/method-notes.html document every assumption, name every source the
  code implements, and declare the tool's limitations.
